<title>UK: Paribas appoints EMU economist.</title>
<headline>Paribas appoints EMU economist.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paribas said on Monday it had appointed Sharda Persaud to its London-based economics team, with specific responsibility for European Economic and Monetary Union (EMU) policy.</p>
<p>Persaud will report to Paribas' chief capital markets economist, Paul Mortimer-Lee, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>Persaud joins from San Paolo Bank, where she was a European economist with responsibility for the UK, German and Italian bond markets, Paribas said.</p>
<p>-- International Bonds Unit +44 171 542 8682</p>
</text>
